# PrismTeX server settings. Copy this file to .env in the directory you start
# the server from (start.sh starts it from the repository root). Every setting
# is optional; the values shown are the defaults. The process environment
# overrides .env.

# Where projects, project state, build output and history live.
# A relative path resolves against the working directory. start.sh uses ./data.
# PRISMTEX_DATA_DIR=data

# Interface and port the API binds.
# PRISMTEX_HOST=127.0.0.1
# PRISMTEX_PORT=8000

# Required when PRISMTEX_HOST is not a loopback address (LAN or Docker).
# Clients send it as "Authorization: Bearer <token>" or the prismtex_token cookie.
# To serve a LAN, also list the server's LAN name or IP in PRISMTEX_ALLOWED_HOSTS
# below (and in PRISMTEX_ALLOWED_ORIGINS for browser writes). In Phase 0 only API
# clients can send the token; the UI binds 127.0.0.1 and has no sign-in yet.
# PRISMTEX_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Extra host names accepted in the Host header, comma-separated.
# localhost, 127.0.0.1 and ::1 are always accepted.
# PRISMTEX_ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# Extra origins (scheme://host[:port]) allowed to send state-changing
# requests, comma-separated. Loopback origins are always allowed.
# PRISMTEX_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# Seconds before a compile is stopped.
# PRISMTEX_COMPILE_TIMEOUT_S=120

# Largest uploaded file, in MB.
# PRISMTEX_MAX_UPLOAD_MB=50

# Largest ZIP import: total unpacked size in MB, and number of files.
# PRISMTEX_IMPORT_MAX_MB=200
# PRISMTEX_IMPORT_MAX_FILES=5000

# The cost ledger of paid model calls: each one is reserved here before it is
# sent and settled after, by the app and by eval runs alike. Keep it outside the
# data directory and back it up, so deleting a data folder never resets the
# count. Unset means <data_dir>/state/ledger.jsonl.
# PRISMTEX_LEDGER_PATH=

# -- The writing agent and its model providers ---------------------------------
# A model ref is ollama:<model>, anthropic:<model> or <preset>:<model>. Unset, a
# Project without its own model uses the first available of: the Ollama default
# (once Ollama reports it pulled), Claude Opus 5.5 (when an Anthropic key is
# set), and the OpenAI-compatible endpoint below.
# PRISMTEX_DEFAULT_MODEL=

# Ollama. NUM_CTX pins the context window of every Ollama model; unset uses the
# catalog's (16384 for qwen3 4B).
# PRISMTEX_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# PRISMTEX_OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=

# Anthropic (paid; needs the cost ledger above). CLAUDE_API_KEY and
# PRISMTEX_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY are other names for the same key, in that order.
# Set FALLBACKS to default for server-side refusal fallback on Opus and Sonnet 5.5.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# CLAUDE_API_KEY=
# PRISMTEX_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# PRISMTEX_ANTHROPIC_FALLBACKS=off

# One OpenAI-compatible endpoint. PRESET is openai or openrouter (paid), vllm
# (needs BASE_URL; serves any OpenAI-compatible server) or lmstudio (defaults to
# http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1). The key is sent only to that preset's base URL;
# OPENAI_API_KEY and other variables meant for other tools are never read.
# PRISMTEX_OPENAI_PRESET=
# PRISMTEX_OPENAI_MODEL=
# PRISMTEX_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# PRISMTEX_OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# The model's context window, in tokens.
# PRISMTEX_OPENAI_CONTEXT=32768
# "input,output" in USD per million tokens. The paid presets need it, and
# setting it meters any endpoint as paid.
# PRISMTEX_OPENAI_PRICE=

# The cost guard for paid models, in USD: a cap per Turn, and an optional
# cumulative stop over the ledger.
# PRISMTEX_MAX_USD_PER_TURN=1.00
# PRISMTEX_COST_STOP_USD=

# 1 keeps the full prompt text in agent Traces.
# PRISMTEX_TRACE_PROMPTS=0

# A fake:scripted script file, for the end-to-end tests only.
# PRISMTEX_FAKE_SCRIPT=
